 "notes": "Stretch 2. Ch. LVIII begins p.103 below the short rule (~y 560) with '1. Re en seset nifu ...'; overline over Re..em (ends before Neter-χert). LVIII numerals: '1.' before Re (p.103 row 1); '2.' p.103 row 3 inside χeper - nek (between D21 and N35/V31); '3.' p.103 row 4 before teken; '4.' p.103 row 6 before ren; '5.' p.104 row 1 inside mat'abet (after owl group, before U28); '6.' p.104 row 3 before em (after qeres-k-tu); '7.' p.104 row 4 inside àuf (between I9 and det F51+Z2). Closing rubric p.104: overline begins over àr (row 5) and runs to row end (emχet); row 6 overline covers pert em only; neter - χert ent not overlined. Ch. LIX p.104 below rule: overline over Re..em (not Neter-χert); short overline over t'eṭ àn in next row. LIX numerals: '1.' before Re (p.104); '2.' p.104 last row after mu (?) before nifu; '3.' p.105 row 1 before suḥt; '4.' p.105 row 2 before seset - s. Stopped p.105 at the rule after 'Ani em maāχeru'. Dots: Budge's English 'likewise ........' (p.104 row 2, under setut) and '................' under qeres - k - tu (p.104 row 3) — recorded as printed. [ni] p.103 row 2 is the only bracketed (restored) group. Budge prints '(sic)' after ṭeni (p.104 row 4 transliteration) and 'mu (?)' (p.104 last row). English 'Assember' (sic, printed so) under saq baiu. No footnotes in the stretch."
